{"id": 4463, "name": "Milan City Park Campground", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://cityofmilantn.com/city-departments/parks-recreation", "lines": ["o play. | The Bobby Ross Amphitheater | | The Bobby Ross Amphitheater is home to many events throughout the year, including Gibson County Relay for Life, 5K races and Milan's Movie in the Park Series. | Reservation Fee: $500 | Utilities Available: Water, Electricity & Restrooms | Pavilions | | The City Park has seven pavilions that can be reserved for a small fee. These pavilions can be used without reservations; how", "ill be posted to our Facebook page every Friday. Please be sure to check that page before planning your weekend gathering at the Park. | Pavilion | Seating | Reservation Fee | Utilities | | Lion's Pavilion | Seats 120 | $60 | Water, Electricity, Restroom | | Sam Crayton Pavilion | Seats 100 | $40 | Water and Electricity | | Jerry Simons Pavilion | Seats 80 | $30 | Water and Electricity | | Nathan Taylor Pavilion | Se", "lion | Seating | Reservation Fee | Utilities | | Lion's Pavilion | Seats 120 | $60 | Water, Electricity, Restroom | | Sam Crayton Pavilion | Seats 100 | $40 | Water and Electricity | | Jerry Simons Pavilion | Seats 80 | $30 | Water and Electricity | | Nathan Taylor Pavilion | Seats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Bennie Ray Moseley Pavilion | Seats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Norman Bryant Pavilion | Se", "Seats 100 | $40 | Water and Electricity | | Jerry Simons Pavilion | Seats 80 | $30 | Water and Electricity | | Nathan Taylor Pavilion | Seats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Bennie Ray Moseley Pavilion | Seats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Norman Bryant Pavilion | Seats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Leonard & Peggy Holbrook | Seats 40 | $20 | None | | Swimming Pool | | The Swimming Pool offers a fu", "ats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Bennie Ray Moseley Pavilion | Seats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Norman Bryant Pavilion | Seats 40 | $20 | Water and Electricity | | Leonard & Peggy Holbrook | Seats 40 | $20 | None | | Swimming Pool | | The Swimming Pool offers a full range of aquatic activities. The pool customarily opens on the mid-May and closes early August. | Must be 16 years old with valid ID to", " City Pool. Any minors, 15 years of age or younger, must be accompanied by an adult atleast 18 years of age with valid ID. | Milan City Pool will be closed on July 4th. | Sunday - Saturday: 12:00 pm - 5:00 pm | Public - $4 per person (4 and under is free) | Swimming trunks and bathing suits MUST be worn while swimming, NO gym shorts. | Pool Parties: | Milan Parks and Recreation Pool Party Application | All applicatio", "time. We have 5 fully accessible sites with a handicap-accessible bath house, water hook ups, 20/30/50 amp service, picnic tables, garbage cans and fire rings. Each lots measures a minimum of 30' x 50'. | Site rental is $25 per night (plus a 4% hotel/motel tax) for a maximum of 14 nights per stay. Only 1 camping unit and 4 people are allowed per camping site. Our office can accept cash or check. We also now have the ", "brand new pickleball courts and a basketball court. Please contact the City Park office to request information regarding court rentals. | Tennis, and Pickleball Court Rentals: | Reservation fees for these facilities are $60/month for one day a week or $100/month for two times a week. Two-hour time slots are available on Sundays, Wednesdays and/or Fridays only. No refunds for rainouts. | All courts are available for t", "e $60/month for one day a week or $100/month for two times a week. Two-hour time slots are available on Sundays, Wednesdays and/or Fridays only. No refunds for rainouts. | All courts are available for tournament rental. $200/day for pickleball or tennis, and an additional $50 can be paid for use of the basketball courts. | A Certificate of Insurance ($1,000,000 minimum coverage) naming the City of Milan as additional", "idays only. No refunds for rainouts. | All courts are available for tournament rental. $200/day for pickleball or tennis, and an additional $50 can be paid for use of the basketball courts. | A Certificate of Insurance ($1,000,000 minimum coverage) naming the City of Milan as additional insured must be provided to the City before any reservation can be held. | Please contact the City Park office to request additional", "ields and two other lighted baseball fields. We also have four lighted softball fields, which an additional softball field that is not lighted. | Baseball and Softball Field Rentals: | Practice fees for travel teams are $60/month for one day a week or $100/month for two times a week from March - October. Two-hour time slots are available on Sundays and/or Wednesdays only. No refunds for rainouts/ | All fields are ava", "ek or $100/month for two times a week from March - October. Two-hour time slots are available on Sundays and/or Wednesdays only. No refunds for rainouts/ | All fields are available for tournament rental. Tournaments are $100 per field, per day. Free day with a 2-day rental (i.e., Friday, Saturday is paid - Sunday is free, if needed) | A Certificate of Insurance ($1,000,000 minimum coverage) naming the City of Milan a", "ainouts/ | All fields are available for tournament rental. Tournaments are $100 per field, per day. Free day with a 2-day rental (i.e., Friday, Saturday is paid - Sunday is free, if needed) | A Certificate of Insurance ($1,000,000 minimum coverage) naming the City of Milan as additional insured must be provided to the City before any reservation can be held. | Please contact the City Park office to request additional"]}, {"url": "https://cityofmilantn.com/images/uploads/content-files/City_of_Milan_RV_Park_Details_and_Rules_5.26.20.pdf", "pdf": true, "via": "here"}]}
{"id": 4464, "name": "Cherokee Park", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://hamblencountytn.gov/cherokee-park/", "lines": ["e 2004-2007 Lakeside Concert Series. | Applications and contracts for use of the amphitheatre can be obtained at the Cherokee Park main office, located in the center of the park. | Rental Rates are as follows: | 1 Day – $500.00 | 2 Days – $900.00 | 3 Days – $1250.00 | If your event is cancelled due to inclement weather, a “rain date” will be provided at no additional cost. | Enclosed Veteran's Pavilion | Cherokee Par", "teran’s Pavilion, will provide adequate space for up to 100 people. The pavilion is air conditioned/heated, has a kitchen facility, and a view of Cherokee Lake. | Rental Rates are as follows: | Hamblen County Residents: $175 per day | Out of County Residents: $225 per day | Wedding/Wedding Receptions $200 per day | Horner Dougherty Pavilion | The largest of the pavilions at Cherokee Park, Horner Dougherty will provid", " find a bbq pit, playground, and horseshoe pit. In front is a gently sloping field that is ideal for children or guests who want to stretch their legs and play. | Rental Rates are as follows: | Hamblen County Residents: $150 per day | Out of County Residents: $200 per day | Weddings/Wedding Receptions $200 per day | Hale-Matney Pavilion | The smaller of the pavilions available, Hale-Matney is ideal for up to 140 gues", "restrooms and a kitchen prep area for your convenience. There is a small playground behind the pavilion and a large open field that is perfect for playing ball. | Rental Rates are as follows: | Hamblen County Residents: $100 per day | Out of Count Residents: $125 per day | Please note that this pavilion is located near the amphitheatre. In the event that the amphitheatre is rented for the same date, it will take prec", "V and connect to the water and electrical hook-ups provided. The campground is equipped with bathrooms and hot showers for campers as well as dump stations for self-contained RV’s. | Rental Rates are as follows: | Sheds $20 per day | RV Hook-up site: Daily /Weekly $35/$175 per day Seniors 62+ $31.50/$157.50 | Monthly Rates 8 Days or More $450 7 Days or Less $350 | Primitive Campsite: $20 per day Senior 62+ $18 per da", "or campers as well as dump stations for self-contained RV’s. | Rental Rates are as follows: | Sheds $20 per day | RV Hook-up site: Daily /Weekly $35/$175 per day Seniors 62+ $31.50/$157.50 | Monthly Rates 8 Days or More $450 7 Days or Less $350 | Primitive Campsite: $20 per day Senior 62+ $18 per day | Prime Lake Access RV Hook-Up Sites Daily/Weekly $45/$225 Seniors 62+ Daily/Weekly $40/$200 Monthly Rates 8 Days or M", "aily /Weekly $35/$175 per day Seniors 62+ $31.50/$157.50 | Monthly Rates 8 Days or More $450 7 Days or Less $350 | Primitive Campsite: $20 per day Senior 62+ $18 per day | Prime Lake Access RV Hook-Up Sites Daily/Weekly $45/$225 Seniors 62+ Daily/Weekly $40/$200 Monthly Rates 8 Days or More $500 7 Days or Less $400 | Off- Season RV Storage November-February $200 monthly | Cherokee Boat Dock | Located at the back of t", "er day Senior 62+ $18 per day | Prime Lake Access RV Hook-Up Sites Daily/Weekly $45/$225 Seniors 62+ Daily/Weekly $40/$200 Monthly Rates 8 Days or More $500 7 Days or Less $400 | Off- Season RV Storage November-February $200 monthly | Cherokee Boat Dock | Located at the back of the park, Cherokee Boat Dock offers slips for rent to house your personal watercraft, bumper boat rides, john boats, 18′ sun trackers, & 24′ ", " boat rides, john boats, 18′ sun trackers, & 24′ deck boats. | Telephone: 423-586-2939 | Winter Hours: 10:00-4:00- Closed Tuesday and Sunday | Summer Hours: 9:00-6:00-Closed Tuesday | Rental Rates are as follows | 8hrs. $275 plus tax and fuel | 4hrs. $150 plus tax and fuel | Weekends and Holidays | 8hrs. $375 plus tax and fuel | 4hrs. $200 plus tax and fuel | Full Day Rental only on Holiday’s | Hourly rentals @ $75/h", "s are as follows | 8hrs. $275 plus tax and fuel | 4hrs. $150 plus tax and fuel | Weekends and Holidays | 8hrs. $375 plus tax and fuel | 4hrs. $200 plus tax and fuel | Full Day Rental only on Holiday’s | Hourly rentals @ $75/hr. with a 2 hour minimum plus taxes and fuel | 24hrs @ $750 plus taxes and fuel | Rentals with a driver if needed. Contact Cherokee Boat Dock for information. | Paddle Boat $15/hr. | (Rates apply", "ntal only on Holiday’s | Hourly rentals @ $75/hr. with a 2 hour minimum plus taxes and fuel | 24hrs @ $750 plus taxes and fuel | Rentals with a driver if needed. Contact Cherokee Boat Dock for information. | Paddle Boat $15/hr. | (Rates apply daily. Rental hours correspond with the Marina hours of operation) | Important Information | Phone: | Pavilion info & reservations (423) 586-5232 | Campground information (423)5", "causing law enforcement to be called to the campground is grounds for eviction from the campground and the park without a refund. | Rent payments are considered late on the 6 th day following the due date. A late fee of $5/day begins on the 6 th day past the due date. | Enforcement of the rules and the decision to evict a camper is at the sole discretion of the Park Manager. Updated 1/1/2025 | ©2020 Hamblen County Te"]}, {"url": "https://hamblencountytn.gov/juvenile-court-services/", "lines": [], "via": "Juvenile Court Services"}, {"url": "https://hamblencountytn.gov/veterans-service-office/", "lines": [], "via": "Veterans Service Office"}]}
